{"type":"message","id":"bd1ad44b","parentId":"5df9a5a0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:59:16.710Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\n- SEO Title: Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sees TON Price Jump 15%\n- Meta Description: The Open Network announced the Toncoin rebrand to Gram, its original name. Founder Pavel Durov confirmed the move, part of the MTGA plan, causing a 15% price surge.\n- URL Slug: toncoin-rebrand-gram-price-surge\n- Categories: Latest News, Trading\n- Primary Keyword: Toncoin Rebrand Gram\n- Secondary Keywords: The Open Network, Pavel Durov, TON Price\n\n---\n\n# Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sparks 15% Price Surge\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** has sent ripples through the market after Telegram founder Pavel Durov announced the network is returning to its original token name. The move, part of a broader strategic initiative, ignited immediate bullish sentiment among traders, causing the price of the native asset to climb over 15% in the hours following the announcement. This strategic pivot signals a new phase for The Open Network, as it aims to fulfill its long-held vision of deep integration within the Telegram messenger application, targeting its massive user base of nearly one billion.\n\nFor traders and long-term holders, the rebranding is more than a simple name change. It represents a deliberate effort by the project's leadership to align with its initial 2018 white paper and reinvigorate its development roadmap. As the ecosystem prepares for this transition over the next three weeks, all eyes will be on the token's market performance and the subsequent milestones laid out in the \"Make TON Great Again\" plan. The event underscores the significant influence that branding and strategic direction can have on a token's valuation in the fast-paced digital asset market.\n\n## A Return to Origins: What is the Gram Rebrand?\n\nThe decision to rebrand Toncoin (TON) to Gram (GRAM) is a direct nod to the project's ambitious beginnings. The name \"Gram\" was first introduced in the original 2018 white paper for the Telegram Open Network. However, the name was shelved after the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) intervened in 2020, blocking the project's $1.7 billion initial coin offering (ICO) and forcing Telegram to distance itself from the project. Now, with Telegram and Durov taking a more direct leadership role since May, the revival of the Gram name symbolizes a full-circle moment for the network.\n\nAccording to a detailed report from [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/369660/ton-price-pumps-telegram-ceo-token-rebranded-gram), the change is purely at the brand level. The underlying blockchain technology will continue to be known as The Open Network (TON). Project leaders have emphasized that no technical migration, token swap, or user action is required. All existing balances, wallet addresses, and smart contracts will function exactly as they did before the name change, ensuring a seamless transition for the entire user base and its integrated applications.\n\n### The Three-Week Transition Plan\n\nPavel Durov outlined that the transition from Toncoin to Gram will unfold over approximately three weeks. This period is designed to allow for a coordinated and orderly update across the ecosystem. Exchanges, wallet providers, and decentralized applications (dApps) that have integrated TON will begin updating their front-end displays and ticker symbols to reflect the new \"Gram\" branding. The gradual rollout aims to prevent market confusion and ensure all participants in the ecosystem are aligned with the new identity. During this phase, traders can expect to see both TON and GRAM tickers used interchangeably on various platforms until the update is universally adopted."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":20,"aggregated":"META\n- SEO Title: Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sees TON Price Jump 15%\n- Meta Description: The Open Network announced the Toncoin rebrand to Gram, its original name. Founder Pavel Durov confirmed the move, part of the MTGA plan, causing a 15% price surge.\n- URL Slug: toncoin-rebrand-gram-price-surge\n- Categories: Latest News, Trading\n- Primary Keyword: Toncoin Rebrand Gram\n- Secondary Keywords: The Open Network, Pavel Durov, TON Price\n\n---\n\n# Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sparks 15% Price Surge\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** has sent ripples through the market after Telegram founder Pavel Durov announced the network is returning to its original token name. The move, part of a broader strategic initiative, ignited immediate bullish sentiment among traders, causing the price of the native asset to climb over 15% in the hours following the announcement. This strategic pivot signals a new phase for The Open Network, as it aims to fulfill its long-held vision of deep integration within the Telegram messenger application, targeting its massive user base of nearly one billion.\n\nFor traders and long-term holders, the rebranding is more than a simple name change. It represents a deliberate effort by the project's leadership to align with its initial 2018 white paper and reinvigorate its development roadmap. As the ecosystem prepares for this transition over the next three weeks, all eyes will be on the token's market performance and the subsequent milestones laid out in the \"Make TON Great Again\" plan. The event underscores the significant influence that branding and strategic direction can have on a token's valuation in the fast-paced digital asset market.\n\n## A Return to Origins: What is the Gram Rebrand?\n\nThe decision to rebrand Toncoin (TON) to Gram (GRAM) is a direct nod to the project's ambitious beginnings. The name \"Gram\" was first introduced in the original 2018 white paper for the Telegram Open Network. However, the name was shelved after the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) intervened in 2020, blocking the project's $1.7 billion initial coin offering (ICO) and forcing Telegram to distance itself from the project. Now, with Telegram and Durov taking a more direct leadership role since May, the revival of the Gram name symbolizes a full-circle moment for the network.\n\nAccording to a detailed report from [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/369660/ton-price-pumps-telegram-ceo-token-rebranded-gram), the change is purely at the brand level. The underlying blockchain technology will continue to be known as The Open Network (TON). Project leaders have emphasized that no technical migration, token swap, or user action is required. All existing balances, wallet addresses, and smart contracts will function exactly as they did before the name change, ensuring a seamless transition for the entire user base and its integrated applications.\n\n### The Three-Week Transition Plan\n\nPavel Durov outlined that the transition from Toncoin to Gram will unfold over approximately three weeks. This period is designed to allow for a coordinated and orderly update across the ecosystem. Exchanges, wallet providers, and decentralized applications (dApps) that have integrated TON will begin updating their front-end displays and ticker symbols to reflect the new \"Gram\" branding. The gradual rollout aims to prevent market confusion and ensure all participants in the ecosystem are aligned with the new identity. During this phase, traders can expect to see both TON and GRAM tickers used interchangeably on various platforms until the update is universally adopted.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780390756710}}
