icted `agentId` to successfully delegate the orchestration tasks.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Monitor the newly created subagent (`agent:main:subagent:1fa2722e-c63d-447a-a950-bfde8843f0c3`) and check the status of the ongoing steps (e.g., Step 2 - Quill article generation, Step 3 - Media generation).\n2. Report pipeline progression and article generation updates back to the user.\n3. Check background process outputs for `openclaw sessions --all-agents` (PID 28385) once execution completes.\n\n## Critical Context\n- The active system runs on WSL2 with local Gateway services routing through Bifrost (`http://192.168.32.1:8888/v1`).\n- The running chat session originates from Telegram (ID: `8726ed77-ce62-4ca7-81f1-d131201150eb`).\n- The directory `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/` acts as the primary hub for pipeline databases (`news_db.sqlite`, `editorial.db`) and step scripts.\n- Current active Pipeline Run ID is `20260602-085601` targeting the TON rebrand back to 'Gram' story.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nThe user (Sawan Bhardwaj) requested to start and manage a content generation and publishing pipeline.\n\n## Early Progress\n- **Session Investigation**: Scanned the OpenClaw environment and identified multiple specialized agents (including `orchestrator`, `researcher`, `writer`, and `publisher`).\n- **Access Restrictions**: Attempted to view cross-agent session histories but was blocked by forbidden access controls.\n- **Pipeline Status Check**: Located the active run directory `/tmp/crypto-run-20260602-085601` targeting a story about Telegram's \"Toncoin\" rebranding to \"Gram\".\n- **Artifact Analysis**: Verified the \"research\" stage succeeded and located a raw article draft (`raw.md` of 10.5 KB), though final output files (`final.md`, `with-image.md`) remain unpopulated (0 bytes).\n\n## Context for Suffix\nThe active pipeline run (`20260602-085601`) is partially complete. The research phase has finished, and a raw artic