rocess (list/poll/log/write/kill/clear/remove) for follow-up."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780390718629,"__openclaw":{"id":"66e4a772","seq":81}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"startcall:default_api:process{action:poll,sessionId:swift-cedar,timeout:5000}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780390718632,"responseId":"QZseao_bJIG90r4P0Zz9-Ak","__openclaw":{"id":"f3aad36a","seq":82}}],"truncated":true,"droppedMessages":false,"contentTruncated":true,"contentRedacted":true,"bytes":15106},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780390985975}}
{"type":"message","id":"f95e0909","parentId":"e7e6021a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:03:07.698Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"tail -n 100 /tmp/crypto-run-20260602-085601/article/final.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":48628,"output":48,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48676,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780390985976,"responseId":"TJwearKLO5G60r4Pit2nmAU"}}
{"type":"message","id":"ac8167e9","parentId":"f95e0909","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:03:07.730Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\n- SEO Title: Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sees TON Price Jump 15%\n- Meta Description: The Open Network announced the Toncoin rebrand to Gram, its original name. Founder Pavel Durov confirmed the move, part of the MTGA plan, causing a 15% price surge.\n- URL Slug: toncoin-rebrand-gram-price-surge\n- Categories: Latest News, Trading\n- Primary Keyword: Toncoin Rebrand Gram\n- Secondary Keywords: The Open Network, Pavel Durov, TON Price\n\n---\n\n# Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sparks 15% Price Surge\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** has ignited the market after Telegram founder Pavel Durov announced the network is returning to its original token name. The move, framed as a return to the project's roots, triggered an immediate 15% price jump, demonstrating a powerful market reaction to the strategic shift. This signals a new phase for The Open Network as it moves to integrate deeply within the Telegram messenger app, a platform with nearly one billion users.\n\nFor traders, this is more than a cosmetic change. It represents a strategic realignment with the project's 2018 white paper and a reinvigoration of its roadmap under Durov's direct leadership. The alignment with Telegram itself provides a distribution channel few other crypto projects can claim. As the ecosystem transitions over the next three weeks, market participants will be watching the token's performance and the execution of the \"Make TON Great Again\" plan.\n\n## A Return to Origins: The Strategy Behind Gram\n\nThe decision to rebrand Toncoin (TON) back to Gram (GRAM) connects the project to its ambitious beginnings. \"Gram\" was the name used in the original 2018 white paper before a 2020 SEC action forced Telegram to abandon its $1.7 billion ICO. With Telegram and Durov taking a more direct leadership role since May, reviving the name symbolizes a full-circle moment for the network and a clear break from its period of uncertainty.\n\nAccording to a report from [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/369660/ton-price-pumps-telegram-ceo-token-rebranded-gram), the change is purely at the brand level. The underlying blockchain technology will continue to be known as The Open Network (TON). No technical migration or token swap is required; all balances, addresses, and smart contracts will function without any change, ensuring a smooth and non-disruptive transition for users and developers.\n\n### The MTGA Roadmap\n\nThis rebranding is the fourth stage of a seven-step roadmap called \"Make TON Great Again\" (MTGA). The plan is a comprehensive strategy to accelerate network growth and solidify its market position. As detailed by [CoinTelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-open-network-ton-native-currency-plans-to-rebrand-to-gram), previous steps included a consensus mechanism upgrade to enhance transaction speed, a significant reduction in network fees, and Telegram replacing the TON Foundation as the network's primary driver. These foundational changes paved the way for the rebrand, signaling the project's renewed ambition and technical readiness for the next phase of growth.\n\n## Market Reacts to Durov's Announcement\n\nThe market responded to the rebranding news with immediate and decisive buying pressure. Following Durov's post on Monday, the price of TON surged more than 15%, climbing from around $1.95 to a peak of $2.26. This sharp rally reflects strong investor confidence in Durov's vision and the strategic direction of the MTGA roadmap. The price action shows how sensitive the market is to fundamental developments involving influential figures, especially one with the track record of the Telegram founder.\n\nAfter the initial spike, the token’s price corrected slightly, consolidating between $2.07 and $2.12 by Tuesday morning. While the excitement was palpable, this shows traders are taking a more measured approach as they evaluate the long-term implications. It is important to note that even with the surge, Gram remains about 74% below its all-time high of $8.25 from June 2024, a peak reached during a short-lived crypto gaming craze. This distance from its peak suggests significant room for potential growth if the network successfully executes its plans and leverages its Telegram integration effectively. The positive short-term sentiment indicates traders see the rebrand as a strong catalyst for future growth, but sustained momentum will depend on tangible progress.\n\n## The Vision for a Telegram Super-App\n\nThe ultimate goal behind the Gram rebrand is to embed The Open Network into the Telegram platform, creating a comprehensive Web3 \"super-app.\" This vision aims to power a seamless experience for Telegram's nearly one billion users, enabling a vast range of decentralized services directly within the messenger. This includes not just global payments, but a rich ecosystem of mini-apps (known as 'tApps'), verifiable digital ownership of assets, and the deployment of sophisticated AI agents.\n\nBy renaming the token to Gram, the project is building a cohesive brand identity to drive mass adoption. The strategy's success depends on the network providing a user-friendly, scalable infrastructure capable of supporting high transaction volumes. If realized, this integration could set a new standard for how blockchain technology interacts with established social platforms, potentially onboarding hundreds of millions of users into Web3 with minimal friction. This represents one of the most significant potential drivers for crypto adoption currently in the market.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** is a pivotal move for The Open Network, marking a return to its original ambitions under Pavel Durov's leadership. This strategic repositioning, not just a cosmetic update, has energized its community and captured renewed investor interest, as shown by the 15% price surge. For traders, the project is now firmly tied to Telegram's strategic vision, a factor that carries immense weight. The coming weeks will be critical to watch how the ecosystem adapts and what the next stages of the MTGA roadmap reveal. This event firmly positions Gram as a key project to monitor, as its success is intertwined with the potential to transform a major global communications platform into a dominant Web3 ecosystem.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. Do I need to swap my TON tokens for GRAM?**\n\nNo, you do not need to do anything. This is a brand change, not a technical migration. Your tokens, address, and balances remain the same. The ticker symbol will simply be updated from TON to GRAM across exchanges and wallets.\n\n**2. Why rebrand back to Gram?**\n\nThe project rebranded to Gram to align with the original name and vision from its 2018 white paper. Leadership calls it a \"return to the roots\" and a key part of the \"Make TON Great Again\" strategy, marking a new chapter of development.\n\n**3. What is the \"Make TON Great Again\" (MTGA) plan?**\n\nThe MTGA plan is a seven-step roadmap to accelerate the growth of The Open Network. The rebrand to Gram is the fourth step, following technical upgrades for speed, lower fees, and Telegram taking a primary leadership role.\n\n**4. How did the price of TON react?**\n\nThe price of TON surged more than 15% within hours of the announcement. It jumped from approximately $1.95 to a high of $2.26 before consolidating slightly."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":10,"aggregated":"META\n- SEO Title: Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sees TON Price Jump 15%\n- Meta Description: The Open Network announced the Toncoin rebrand to Gram, its original name. Founder Pavel Durov confirmed the move, part of the MTGA plan, causing a 15% price surge.\n- URL Slug: toncoin-rebrand-gram-price-surge\n- Categories: Latest News, Trading\n- Primary Keyword: Toncoin Rebrand Gram\n- Secondary Keywords: The Open Network, Pavel Durov, TON Price\n\n---\n\n# Toncoin Rebrand to Gram Sparks 15% Price Surge\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** has ignited the market after Telegram founder Pavel Durov announced the network is returning to its original token name. The move, framed as a return to the project's roots, triggered an immediate 15% price jump, demonstrating a powerful market reaction to the strategic shift. This signals a new phase for The Open Network as it moves to integrate deeply within the Telegram messenger app, a platform with nearly one billion users.\n\nFor traders, this is more than a cosmetic change. It represents a strategic realignment with the project's 2018 white paper and a reinvigoration of its roadmap under Durov's direct leadership. The alignment with Telegram itself provides a distribution channel few other crypto projects can claim. As the ecosystem transitions over the next three weeks, market participants will be watching the token's performance and the execution of the \"Make TON Great Again\" plan.\n\n## A Return to Origins: The Strategy Behind Gram\n\nThe decision to rebrand Toncoin (TON) back to Gram (GRAM) connects the project to its ambitious beginnings. \"Gram\" was the name used in the original 2018 white paper before a 2020 SEC action forced Telegram to abandon its $1.7 billion ICO. With Telegram and Durov taking a more direct leadership role since May, reviving the name symbolizes a full-circle moment for the network and a clear break from its period of uncertainty.\n\nAccording to a report from [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/369660/ton-price-pumps-telegram-ceo-token-rebranded-gram), the change is purely at the brand level. The underlying blockchain technology will continue to be known as The Open Network (TON). No technical migration or token swap is required; all balances, addresses, and smart contracts will function without any change, ensuring a smooth and non-disruptive transition for users and developers.\n\n### The MTGA Roadmap\n\nThis rebranding is the fourth stage of a seven-step roadmap called \"Make TON Great Again\" (MTGA). The plan is a comprehensive strategy to accelerate network growth and solidify its market position. As detailed by [CoinTelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-open-network-ton-native-currency-plans-to-rebrand-to-gram), previous steps included a consensus mechanism upgrade to enhance transaction speed, a significant reduction in network fees, and Telegram replacing the TON Foundation as the network's primary driver. These foundational changes paved the way for the rebrand, signaling the project's renewed ambition and technical readiness for the next phase of growth.\n\n## Market Reacts to Durov's Announcement\n\nThe market responded to the rebranding news with immediate and decisive buying pressure. Following Durov's post on Monday, the price of TON surged more than 15%, climbing from around $1.95 to a peak of $2.26. This sharp rally reflects strong investor confidence in Durov's vision and the strategic direction of the MTGA roadmap. The price action shows how sensitive the market is to fundamental developments involving influential figures, especially one with the track record of the Telegram founder.\n\nAfter the initial spike, the token’s price corrected slightly, consolidating between $2.07 and $2.12 by Tuesday morning. While the excitement was palpable, this shows traders are taking a more measured approach as they evaluate the long-term implications. It is important to note that even with the surge, Gram remains about 74% below its all-time high of $8.25 from June 2024, a peak reached during a short-lived crypto gaming craze. This distance from its peak suggests significant room for potential growth if the network successfully executes its plans and leverages its Telegram integration effectively. The positive short-term sentiment indicates traders see the rebrand as a strong catalyst for future growth, but sustained momentum will depend on tangible progress.\n\n## The Vision for a Telegram Super-App\n\nThe ultimate goal behind the Gram rebrand is to embed The Open Network into the Telegram platform, creating a comprehensive Web3 \"super-app.\" This vision aims to power a seamless experience for Telegram's nearly one billion users, enabling a vast range of decentralized services directly within the messenger. This includes not just global payments, but a rich ecosystem of mini-apps (known as 'tApps'), verifiable digital ownership of assets, and the deployment of sophisticated AI agents.\n\nBy renaming the token to Gram, the project is building a cohesive brand identity to drive mass adoption. The strategy's success depends on the network providing a user-friendly, scalable infrastructure capable of supporting high transaction volumes. If realized, this integration could set a new standard for how blockchain technology interacts with established social platforms, potentially onboarding hundreds of millions of users into Web3 with minimal friction. This represents one of the most significant potential drivers for crypto adoption currently in the market.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe **Toncoin rebrand to Gram** is a pivotal move for The Open Network, marking a return to its original ambitions under Pavel Durov's leadership. This strategic repositioning, not just a cosmetic update, has energized its community and captured renewed investor interest, as shown by the 15% price surge. For traders, the project is now firmly tied to Telegram's strategic vision, a factor that carries immense weight. The coming weeks will be critical to watch how the ecosystem adapts and what the next stages of the MTGA roadmap reveal. This event firmly positions Gram as a key project to monitor, as its success is intertwined with the potential to transform a major global communications platform into a dominant Web3 ecosystem.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. Do I need to swap my TON tokens for GRAM?**\n\nNo, you do not need to do anything. This is a brand change, not a technical migration. Your tokens, address, and balances remain the same. The ticker symbol will simply be updated from TON to GRAM across exchanges and wallets.\n\n**2. Why rebrand back to Gram?**\n\nThe project rebranded to Gram to align with the original name and vision from its 2018 white paper. Leadership calls it a \"return to the roots\" and a key part of the \"Make TON Great Again\" strategy, marking a new chapter of development.\n\n**3. What is the \"Make TON Great Again\" (MTGA) plan?**\n\nThe MTGA plan is a seven-step roadmap to accelerate the growth of The Open Network. The rebrand to Gram is the fourth step, following technical upgrades for speed, lower fees, and Telegram taking a primary leadership role.\n\n**4. How did the price of TON react?**\n\nThe price of TON surged more than 15% within hours of the announcement. It jumped from approximately $1.95 to a high of $2.26 before consolidating slightly.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780390987729}}
